<!DOCTYPE html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<pre class="metadata">
title: Intl.LocaleMatcher
stage: 1
contributors: Ecma International, Long Ho
location: https://tc39.es/proposal-intl-localematcher/
</pre>
<emu-biblio href="./node_modules/@tc39/ecma262-biblio/biblio.json"></emu-biblio>
<emu-biblio href="./node_modules/@tc39/ecma402-biblio/biblio.json"></emu-biblio>

<emu-intro id="sec-introduction">
  <h1>Introduction</h1>
  <p>This working draft prepares application-supplied locales once and matches requests without implicit defaulting. Best-fit policy and data remain implementation-defined.</p>
  <p>In <a href="https://tc39.es/ecma402/#sec-constructor-properties-of-the-intl-object">Constructor Properties of the Intl Object</a>, add Intl.LocaleMatcher and exclude it, alongside Intl.Locale, from the service constructors. It matches application resources rather than negotiating an implementation's supported services.</p>
</emu-intro>

<emu-clause id="localematcher-objects">
  <h1>LocaleMatcher Objects</h1>
  <p>The objects and functions defined here follow ECMA-402's <a href="https://tc39.es/ecma402/#requirements">requirements for standard built-in ECMAScript objects</a>.</p>

  <emu-clause id="sec-intl-localematcher-constructor">
    <h1>The Intl.LocaleMatcher Constructor</h1>
    <p>The Intl.LocaleMatcher constructor is <dfn>%Intl.LocaleMatcher%</dfn>, the initial value of the *"LocaleMatcher"* property of the Intl object.</p>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher ( _availableLocales_ [ , _options_ ] )</h1>
      <emu-alg>
        1. If NewTarget is *undefined*, throw a *TypeError* exception.
        1. Let _slots_ be « [[InitializedLocaleMatcher]], [[AvailableLocales]], [[LocaleMatcher]] ».
        1. Let _matcher_ be ? OrdinaryCreateFromConstructor(NewTarget, *"%Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype%"*, _slots_).
        1. Let _available_ be ? CanonicalizeLocaleList(_availableLocales_).
        1. For each element _locale_ of _available_, do
          1. If _locale_ contains a Unicode locale extension sequence, throw a *RangeError* exception.
        1. Set _options_ to ? GetOptionsObject(_options_).
        1. Let _algorithm_ be ? GetOption(_options_, *"algorithm"*, ~string~, « *"lookup"*, *"best fit"* », *"best fit"*).
        1. Set _matcher_.[[AvailableLocales]] to _available_.
        1. Set _matcher_.[[LocaleMatcher]] to _algorithm_.
        1. Set _matcher_.[[InitializedLocaleMatcher]] to *true*.
        1. Return _matcher_.
      </emu-alg>
      <p>The *"length"* property of Intl.LocaleMatcher is *1*<sub>𝔽</sub>.</p>
      <emu-note>
        Available locales describe app resources. No host default, parent tags, or Intl service support is required. CanonicalizeLocaleList copies and deduplicates them; later input or option mutations do not change the matcher. Implementations may prepare reusable indices, without a required technique or timing guarantee.
      </emu-note>
    </emu-clause>
  </emu-clause>

  <emu-clause id="sec-properties-of-intl-localematcher-constructor">
    <h1>Properties of the Intl.LocaleMatcher Constructor</h1>
    <p>The constructor has a [[Prototype]] internal slot whose value is %Function.prototype%.</p>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher.prototype">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype</h1>
      <p>The value of this property is %Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype%.</p>
      <p>This property has the attributes { [[Writable]]: *false*, [[Enumerable]]: *false*, [[Configurable]]: *false* }.</p>
    </emu-clause>
  </emu-clause>

  <emu-clause id="sec-properties-of-intl-localematcher-prototype-object">
    <h1>Properties of the Intl.LocaleMatcher Prototype Object</h1>
    <p>The prototype object is <dfn>%Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype%</dfn>, an ordinary object with [[Prototype]] %Object.prototype%. It is not a LocaleMatcher instance and has none of the instance internal slots.</p>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher.prototype.constructor">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype.constructor</h1>
      <p>The initial value is %Intl.LocaleMatcher%.</p>
    </emu-clause>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher.prototype.match">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype.match ( _requestedLocales_ )</h1>
      <emu-alg>
        1. Let _matcher_ be the *this* value.
        1. Perform ? RequireInternalSlot(_matcher_, [[InitializedLocaleMatcher]]).
        1. Let _requested_ be ? CanonicalizeLocaleList(_requestedLocales_).
        1. Let _available_ be _matcher_.[[AvailableLocales]].
        1. If _requested_ is empty or _available_ is empty, return *undefined*.
        1. If _matcher_.[[LocaleMatcher]] is *"lookup"*, then
          1. Let _match_ be LookupMatchingLocaleByPrefix(_available_, _requested_).
        1. Else,
          1. Let _match_ be LookupMatchingLocaleByBestFit(_available_, _requested_).
        1. If _match_ is *undefined*, return *undefined*.
        1. Return _match_.[[locale]].
      </emu-alg>
      <p>The *"length"* property of this method is *1*<sub>𝔽</sub>.</p>
      <emu-note>
        Each call validates the complete request list, even with no available locales. No match returns undefined; callers can apply their own fallback. This method does not call DefaultLocale or copy requested Unicode locale extensions into the result.
      </emu-note>
      <emu-note>
        Best fit uses the existing ECMA-402 operation, with no required CLDR/ICU data, scoring, expansion, penalty, or tie policy. Other extensions and private-use subtags retain that operation's treatment; no application-specific meaning is assigned.
      </emu-note>
    </emu-clause>

    <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher.prototype-tostringtag">
      <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher.prototype [ %Symbol.toStringTag% ]</h1>
      <p>The initial value is *"Intl.LocaleMatcher"*.</p>
      <p>This property has the attributes { [[Writable]]: *false*, [[Enumerable]]: *false*, [[Configurable]]: *true* }.</p>
    </emu-clause>
  </emu-clause>

  <emu-clause id="sec-properties-of-intl-localematcher-instances">
    <h1>Properties of Intl.LocaleMatcher Instances</h1>
    <p>Instances are ordinary objects with these internal slots:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>[[InitializedLocaleMatcher]]: *true*.</li>
      <li>[[AvailableLocales]]: the private Available Locales List copied during construction.</li>
      <li>[[LocaleMatcher]]: *"lookup"* or *"best fit"*.</li>
    </ul>
  </emu-clause>
</emu-clause>
